<blockquote class="uncited"><div><blockquote class="uncited"><div><blockquote class="uncited"><div>There is no official tyt firmware on tyt site, not for uv390 10w</div></blockquote>I saved some 10W firmware files that was posted earlier, but there is no CPS in that ZIP <br><br><a href="https://www.sa0bux.se/Ham/MDUV380-390-plus/" class="postlink">https://www.sa0bux.se/Ham/MDUV380-390-plus/</a></div></blockquote>CPS will be the same as the 5W version<br><br>Note. The Flash memory will have non-official data in it and the radio will probably give the message about being locked, so they will need to upload a blank codeplug with no PIN number, and also to do this they will need to edit the CPS ini file to allow upload to a locked radio.<br><br>I can't remember the exact changes to settings, I think its <br><br>change <br><br>password=0 <br><br>to<br><br>password=password</div></blockquote>I tried your files, it seems it "worked" but the radio says Unprogrammed and cant do anything on it. Does this mean its being locked?<br>If it means its locked like you said, how do I unlock it step by step? I have read what you said but dont quite understand what and where to do.<br><br>EDIT: I tried uploading blank codeplug, and I got into the radio, but seems weird and buggy, also Im missing program radio option. I also get short static noise 50% of times when I click "menu" button, anyone familiar with that?<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=7115">YU4MSF</a> — Sat Oct 19, 2024 3:08 pm</p><hr />
